1
00:00:05,571 --> 00:00:07,271
(All characters, organizations,
and events in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,271 --> 00:00:08,805
(Filming complied with guidelines
for children, youth, and animals.)

3
00:00:09,739 --> 00:00:13,026
The man you're nice to and take care of,
can't it just be me?

4
00:00:15,458 --> 00:00:17,691
I don't understand...

5
00:00:18,258 --> 00:00:21,158
You really don't get it, do you?

6
00:00:23,725 --> 00:00:27,491
Right now, I'm confessing.

7
00:00:27,925 --> 00:00:31,591
Just look at me.

8
00:00:34,058 --> 00:00:37,258
I think I've fallen for you. Gyu Rim.

9
00:00:37,558 --> 00:00:38,891
Now do you get it?

10
00:00:43,025 --> 00:00:47,525
Just like that, out of nowhere?

11
00:00:50,258 --> 00:00:54,158
Falling for someone can take
all of ten seconds.

12
00:00:54,825 --> 00:00:57,358
Still, I don't think this is right.

13
00:01:00,158 --> 00:01:02,858
What's not right? Why isn't it?

14
00:01:03,625 --> 00:01:05,825
Are you angry with me right now?

15
00:01:06,925 --> 00:01:10,025
No, I'm not angry...

16
00:01:12,891 --> 00:01:15,191
You call this an ordinary coincidence?

17
00:01:15,958 --> 00:01:19,425
Think about it.
Our 59.9 dollars, six shirts.

18
00:01:20,325 --> 00:01:23,858
What are the odds of wearing the same one
three days straight out of six?

19
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,066
One in six times one in six is one in 36,
then one in 216.

20
00:01:28,091 --> 00:01:31,725
Same hour, same bus, and now the same job.

21
00:01:31,791 --> 00:01:33,891
Isn't that amazing? What a coincidence.

22
00:01:38,878 --> 00:01:43,078
And just so there's no misunderstanding,
let me add one thing,

23
00:01:43,191 --> 00:01:47,325
I don't just fall for anyone,
confess, and come on strong like this.

24
00:01:47,325 --> 00:01:48,625
That's not who I am.

25
00:01:49,851 --> 00:01:53,094
If I don't tell you how I feel now,

26
00:01:53,458 --> 00:01:58,391
I felt like I'd lose you for good.
My heart's pounding right now...

27
00:01:58,525 --> 00:02:00,291
This took real courage.

28
00:02:02,204 --> 00:02:04,799
I'm not asking for an answer right now.

29
00:02:05,411 --> 00:02:08,186
Take your time and think it over,

30
00:02:09,029 --> 00:02:16,019
and if you ever think, "Dating this guy
might actually be fun,"

31
00:02:16,344 --> 00:02:21,310
then tell me anytime. All right?

32
00:02:24,958 --> 00:02:26,858
I'll tell you now.

33
00:02:28,791 --> 00:02:32,391
I'm truly grateful
that you think so well of me.

34
00:02:33,391 --> 00:02:39,991
But right now I don't have the time,
the room, or the heart to date anyone.

35
00:02:46,125 --> 00:02:47,691
Are you turning me down?

36
00:02:47,991 --> 00:02:48,991
Yes.

37
00:02:49,625 --> 00:02:51,358
- Just like that?
- Yes.

38
00:02:51,691 --> 00:02:54,891
Flat out? Without even thinking?

39
00:02:55,591 --> 00:02:58,791
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

40
00:02:58,991 --> 00:03:00,258
I'm sorry.

41
00:03:15,165 --> 00:03:20,398
Three apologies? She is only
making me feel worse.

42
00:03:56,958 --> 00:03:58,458
- Can we order?
- Excuse me?

43
00:03:58,637 --> 00:03:59,763
Go ahead.

44
00:04:09,051 --> 00:04:10,151
Excuse me.

45
00:04:12,158 --> 00:04:15,091
Yes. Do you need something?

46
00:04:15,116 --> 00:04:17,216
- Clear this, please.
- Yes, sir.

47
00:04:29,991 --> 00:04:34,725
If you do that again, I'll file
a formal complaint.

48
00:04:38,337 --> 00:04:40,517
See? I told you.

49
00:04:41,364 --> 00:04:43,564
Yeah, her skin is so soft.

50
00:04:43,704 --> 00:04:46,671
She said she'd file
a formal complaint next time.

51
00:04:47,017 --> 00:04:49,314
Just deny it, idiot.
It's not our first time.

52
00:04:49,418 --> 00:04:50,485
You okay?

53
00:04:51,844 --> 00:04:52,844
Did he touch your hand?

54
00:04:53,005 --> 00:04:57,905
Next time she comes over, want to spill
juice on her and play it off?

55
00:04:57,931 --> 00:05:01,933
- I like that.
- A chance to check her out?

56
00:05:02,791 --> 00:05:04,758
- Then how about a bet?
- What?

57
00:05:04,783 --> 00:05:08,049
Closest guess eats for free.

58
00:05:08,325 --> 00:05:10,991
- Deal.
- Take a look.

59
00:05:11,091 --> 00:05:16,525
- I say a full B cup.
- No way.

60
00:05:17,025 --> 00:05:20,358
- Are you dumb? It's 34B.
- No, there's nothing there.

61
00:05:20,391 --> 00:05:21,891
- Did you feel it?
- It's all padding.

62
00:05:21,891 --> 00:05:23,391
- I said no.
- It's 34B.

63
00:05:23,425 --> 00:05:26,725
- 34B!
- Don't you two know the alphabet?

64
00:05:32,391 --> 00:05:34,391
Are you out of your mind?

65
00:05:45,571 --> 00:05:48,103
- Hey, look at me.
- I'm sorry.

66
00:05:48,818 --> 00:05:50,151
I can't even speak now.

67
00:05:50,257 --> 00:05:53,751
Forget it. No settlement.

68
00:05:53,957 --> 00:05:56,558
His uncle is high up
in the prosecutors' office.

69
00:05:56,858 --> 00:06:00,091
- Call him and get this punk locked up!
- Right.

70
00:06:00,091 --> 00:06:02,458
Call the Moon Bear of Mapo,

71
00:06:02,458 --> 00:06:06,125
the Bulldog of Yongsan,
the Viper of Wangsimni,

72
00:06:06,125 --> 00:06:07,958
and have them work this punk over.

73
00:06:07,958 --> 00:06:09,458
Yeah, should we?

74
00:06:09,504 --> 00:06:11,833
Should we end this guy's life for good?

75
00:06:11,858 --> 00:06:14,458
Go ahead. Call them. Call them all.

76
00:06:14,558 --> 00:06:18,658
Prosecutors, police, bears, bulldogs,
vipers, every animal you know.

77
00:06:18,758 --> 00:06:19,891
You'd better call them.

78
00:06:19,891 --> 00:06:21,991
Or I'll throw you in a zoo cage
right along with them.

79
00:06:21,991 --> 00:06:23,291
Kim Mu Jin!

80
00:06:25,125 --> 00:06:27,825
I'm not settling with trash like you,
so let's take this outside.

81
00:06:27,825 --> 00:06:29,558
Well? Who wants to go first?

82
00:06:29,691 --> 00:06:31,680
One-on-one, or all of you at once?

83
00:06:31,705 --> 00:06:32,866
Either works. Let's go.

84
00:06:32,891 --> 00:06:35,191
I'll cover every hospital bill. Come on.

85
00:06:35,191 --> 00:06:36,858
Let's go. Get out here!

86
00:06:36,904 --> 00:06:38,949
All of you! Come on!

87
00:07:39,958 --> 00:07:42,925
"A customer may act up,"

88
00:07:43,125 --> 00:07:47,425
"but the customer is king.
Is he insane, hitting a customer?"

89
00:07:50,365 --> 00:07:53,124
That's what the manager said,

90
00:07:54,158 --> 00:07:59,058
so I said I'd report it to the police
myself, as the victim.

91
00:08:00,243 --> 00:08:04,643
And I'd report her to head office
for failing to protect her staff.

92
00:08:08,324 --> 00:08:11,312
The manager went pale, of course,

93
00:08:11,448 --> 00:08:14,136
and those customers ran off
without looking back.

94
00:08:19,391 --> 00:08:21,191
I'm not made of iron.

95
00:08:23,638 --> 00:08:25,271
I'm not made of stone either.

96
00:08:28,471 --> 00:08:32,451
When someone looks out for me,
treats me well,

97
00:08:33,978 --> 00:08:36,661
and cares about me, it moves me too.

98
00:08:38,058 --> 00:08:39,791
I'm only human.

99
00:08:43,191 --> 00:08:46,925
What does that mean?

100
00:08:50,138 --> 00:08:51,438
I'm saying...

101
00:08:53,591 --> 00:08:57,434
that my heart flutters for you too.

102
00:09:05,825 --> 00:09:07,325
Then are we...

103
00:09:08,758 --> 00:09:10,125
dating now?

104
00:09:15,825 --> 00:09:18,158
I go to bed at midnight, up at four.

105
00:09:18,191 --> 00:09:20,868
Three and a half hours delivering juice,

106
00:09:21,198 --> 00:09:25,576
then home to wake the kids, get them
ready for school, feed them breakfast,

107
00:09:25,858 --> 00:09:30,458
once they're gone, dishes, laundry,
vacuuming, mopping.

108
00:09:30,691 --> 00:09:33,525
Then straight to a six-hour shift,
and after that,

109
00:09:33,525 --> 00:09:35,891
straight to the next one
for five more hours.

110
00:09:36,025 --> 00:09:40,325
Home again, tidy up, shower,

111
00:09:40,325 --> 00:09:43,725
pass out, then it's up at 4 a.m.
all over again.

112
00:09:45,477 --> 00:09:49,509
There isn't one hour in my day
that belongs to me,

113
00:09:49,668 --> 00:09:51,935
and no room for you in it either.

114
00:09:52,958 --> 00:09:56,058
So please stop stirring me up.

115
00:09:56,651 --> 00:10:00,717
Don't be kind. Don't be warm.

116
00:10:00,989 --> 00:10:03,823
Don't get angry on my behalf like this.

117
00:10:04,784 --> 00:10:07,584
No more and no less,

118
00:10:09,158 --> 00:10:11,458
just treat me like a coworker.

119
00:10:41,791 --> 00:10:47,706
Bravo. Well done. He set them straight.

120
00:10:47,731 --> 00:10:50,324
Men like that shouldn't be tolerated.

121
00:10:50,684 --> 00:10:56,166
Secretary Cha, and not just because he's
my son, but isn't Mu Jin magnificent?

122
00:10:56,191 --> 00:10:58,107
Yes, ma'am.

123
00:10:58,958 --> 00:11:04,478
Was Mu Jin always the type
to stand up for what's right like that?

124
00:11:06,630 --> 00:11:10,130
Once people learn he's my son,

125
00:11:10,191 --> 00:11:14,225
- it'll do wonders for his image, right?
- Yes, I believe so.

126
00:11:15,158 --> 00:11:18,225
I won't praise or scold him over today.

127
00:11:18,225 --> 00:11:20,325
Act as if I was never briefed.

128
00:11:20,391 --> 00:11:23,291
- I know nothing.
- Understood. Excuse me.

129
00:11:24,091 --> 00:11:31,025
Is there anything between Mu Jin
and that part-timer who was harassed?

130
00:11:31,185 --> 00:11:33,118
Kim Yun Jin!

131
00:11:35,323 --> 00:11:39,595
That look on your face says
I hit the nail on the head.

132
00:11:41,425 --> 00:11:44,402
Is that part-timer really dating Mu Jin?

133
00:11:45,451 --> 00:11:47,185
I'll look into it.

134
00:11:47,492 --> 00:11:52,025
If you know something, tell me the truth.

135
00:11:54,391 --> 00:11:57,248
The manager does suspect as much...

136
00:11:57,525 --> 00:12:00,658
I'll look into it quickly
and report back accurately.

137
00:12:04,857 --> 00:12:09,724
Interesting. That part-timer
must be no ordinary girl.

138
00:12:10,331 --> 00:12:13,026
He's only been working there a few days.

139
00:12:14,209 --> 00:12:16,717
How did she turn his head so fast?

140
00:12:18,670 --> 00:12:21,670
Dating a part-timer?

141
00:12:22,811 --> 00:12:25,602
That stuck-up brat?

142
00:12:55,671 --> 00:12:57,171
It's so late.

143
00:12:59,591 --> 00:13:01,491
Let me cook you something.

144
00:13:02,357 --> 00:13:04,270
Ta-da.

145
00:13:05,225 --> 00:13:06,825
It's chicken. Chicken!

146
00:13:07,609 --> 00:13:09,158
Ta-da.

147
00:13:09,604 --> 00:13:13,348
Han Gyu Min, Han Gyu Seo, wake up.

148
00:13:13,917 --> 00:13:17,708
Brush your teeth and wash up
before bed. Up you get.

149
00:13:17,771 --> 00:13:22,804
Come on, up. Go wash up!

150
00:13:27,751 --> 00:13:31,360
No half-brushing. Top and bottom,
every corner. You know the drill.

151
00:13:31,398 --> 00:13:33,431
I'll be inspecting later.

152
00:13:50,483 --> 00:13:54,017
There's nothing
in that fridge worth eating.

153
00:13:54,411 --> 00:13:59,744
Next time, make some tuna kimchi stew.
It's my favorite. Be a good daughter.

154
00:13:59,917 --> 00:14:02,784
That's how good things come to you.
From your father.

155
00:14:14,591 --> 00:14:20,057
Gyu Rim! I brushed and washed up
and put on all my cream.

156
00:14:20,082 --> 00:14:25,655
Really? Let me see. All clean.

157
00:14:25,710 --> 00:14:27,470
Time for bed, Gyu Seo. Lie down.

158
00:14:33,544 --> 00:14:36,744
- Good night, Gyu Seo. Sweet dreams.
- Okay!

159
00:14:48,371 --> 00:14:50,703
Han Gyu O, where are you?

160
00:14:51,058 --> 00:14:55,825
I'll stay up until you're home,
so come back and let's talk.

161
00:15:07,977 --> 00:15:14,944
A guy who only drinks fine wine
and whiskey, on convenience store beer?

162
00:15:15,311 --> 00:15:18,511
Are you enjoying slumming it lately?

163
00:15:18,957 --> 00:15:20,690
I told Han Gyu Rim how I feel.

164
00:15:23,725 --> 00:15:25,658
Which Han Gyu Rim?

165
00:15:26,670 --> 00:15:29,204
The one who gave me her lunchbox?

166
00:15:29,558 --> 00:15:33,858
The one I asked you to introduce me to,
the one time ever, and you refused?

167
00:15:37,517 --> 00:15:40,125
So?

168
00:15:43,658 --> 00:15:45,458
How did it go?

169
00:15:50,825 --> 00:15:52,025
She turned me down.

170
00:16:00,611 --> 00:16:04,333
That's the funniest thing
I've heard all year.

171
00:16:04,358 --> 00:16:06,007
Serves you right!

172
00:16:07,625 --> 00:16:10,383
Fine. Laugh all you want.

173
00:16:17,010 --> 00:16:18,861
Why'd she turn you down?

174
00:16:20,058 --> 00:16:21,967
She said it didn't feel right.

175
00:16:22,957 --> 00:16:24,857
What didn't?

176
00:16:26,197 --> 00:16:32,366
Fair enough. A man this good-looking
puts women off. Too much pressure.

177
00:16:32,391 --> 00:16:33,758
Makes them uneasy, too.

178
00:16:33,891 --> 00:16:39,934
An average-looking guy like me
is easy to be around.

179
00:16:41,957 --> 00:16:47,898
She says she doesn't have the time,

180
00:16:48,408 --> 00:16:49,777
or headspace to date anyone.

181
00:16:50,517 --> 00:16:53,066
How can anyone be too busy to date?

182
00:16:53,091 --> 00:16:56,258
Should I just tell her I'm loaded?

183
00:16:56,258 --> 00:16:58,663
No, that I'm the heir to a fortune?

184
00:16:59,538 --> 00:17:02,471
Should I tell her
I'll give her the space she needs?

185
00:17:03,691 --> 00:17:05,325
That she can leave it all to me.

186
00:17:05,350 --> 00:17:07,525
Have you lost your mind?

187
00:17:07,591 --> 00:17:09,958
- That's cheating.
- How is it?

188
00:17:09,958 --> 00:17:12,591
I don't go around bragging
about my dad's abalone farm.

189
00:17:13,825 --> 00:17:16,358
And frankly, the wealth isn't even yours.

190
00:17:16,591 --> 00:17:18,958
You haven't inherited a thing yet.

191
00:17:21,804 --> 00:17:23,071
You're right.

192
00:17:24,932 --> 00:17:29,296
But when she says not to stir her up,

193
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:31,754
not to pay her any attention,

194
00:17:32,091 --> 00:17:35,925
why does it only sound like
"pay me more attention, stir me up?"

195
00:17:35,950 --> 00:17:39,983
That's you running everything
through a rose-colored filter.

196
00:17:41,291 --> 00:17:43,825
Do as she said. Don't stir her up.

197
00:17:44,158 --> 00:17:45,825
Not when you can't follow through.

198
00:17:46,225 --> 00:17:48,358
Why couldn't I follow through?

199
00:17:48,544 --> 00:17:51,244
Why are you shouting all of a sudden?

200
00:17:51,517 --> 00:17:54,017
- Caught you just wanting some fun?
- What?

201
00:17:54,691 --> 00:17:57,758
So you wanted a blind date just for fun?

202
00:17:58,058 --> 00:18:02,333
- Are you insane?
- Please. Am I you? Are we the same?

203
00:18:02,358 --> 00:18:03,858
You and I are different.

204
00:18:04,191 --> 00:18:08,216
I'm better looking, richer, smarter,
and I have more hair.

205
00:18:08,241 --> 00:18:12,598
Don't you get it? That's your curse,
your own barrier.

206
00:18:13,491 --> 00:18:19,983
I'm not the eldest son or an heir,
so there's no company waiting for me.

207
00:18:20,410 --> 00:18:25,166
And my mom would welcome
whoever I brought home.

208
00:18:25,191 --> 00:18:27,691
But your mother wouldn't.

209
00:18:29,150 --> 00:18:32,979
Honestly, what her parents do,

210
00:18:33,025 --> 00:18:37,091
where she went to school, her job,
what her siblings do,

211
00:18:37,291 --> 00:18:39,225
isn't it normal for the chairwoman
to weigh all that?

212
00:18:39,325 --> 00:18:40,458
Don't you see that?

213
00:18:44,971 --> 00:18:45,992
You're right.

214
00:18:47,486 --> 00:18:49,944
You're absolutely right.

215
00:18:50,791 --> 00:18:55,016
- Thanks. That was well said.
- When have I not been right?

216
00:18:57,331 --> 00:19:00,760
When he runs out of words,
he always smacks me upside the head.

217
00:19:00,931 --> 00:19:05,615
It was a strange place where signs
made of chocolate melted away.

218
00:19:10,329 --> 00:19:13,933
Are you so ignorant
you can't even read English?

219
00:19:13,958 --> 00:19:16,358
Don't you know "dry clean only?"

220
00:19:20,358 --> 00:19:23,000
- Only dry...
- Even a grade-schooler knows that.

221
00:19:23,025 --> 00:19:24,558
Are you actually a birdbrain?

222
00:19:24,625 --> 00:19:26,925
Didn't I say this had to go
to the dry cleaners?

223
00:19:26,925 --> 00:19:30,569
How could you put it in the washer?
Do you know what this cost?

224
00:19:30,758 --> 00:19:31,958
I'm sorry.

225
00:19:32,064 --> 00:19:33,998
I was rushing and didn't check.

226
00:19:34,264 --> 00:19:35,497
Was it very expensive?

227
00:19:35,644 --> 00:19:38,355
More than you make in a month. Satisfied?

228
00:19:39,438 --> 00:19:43,598
Time for bed, Gyu Min. I'll read
the rest tomorrow. Good night.

229
00:19:44,697 --> 00:19:47,331
How are you paying for this?

230
00:19:49,757 --> 00:19:52,445
She needs to sleep.
Keep it down and come out.

231
00:19:57,491 --> 00:19:59,234
Seriously...

232
00:20:01,330 --> 00:20:03,263
You ruined it, so you pay for it.

233
00:20:03,525 --> 00:20:07,291
Pay me 1,500 dollars right now, or fix it.

234
00:20:07,791 --> 00:20:10,158
How can one blouse cost that much?

235
00:20:10,425 --> 00:20:12,725
What blouse costs 1,500 dollars?

236
00:20:12,725 --> 00:20:14,091
Right here.

237
00:20:14,191 --> 00:20:17,258
Not in your world, maybe,
but they exist in mine.

238
00:20:17,258 --> 00:20:19,225
So how are you paying for it?

239
00:20:20,218 --> 00:20:23,118
I don't have that money. I can't.

240
00:20:25,770 --> 00:20:28,437
Take whatever you want
from my clothes instead.

241
00:20:30,291 --> 00:20:32,016
Why would I wear your clothes?

242
00:20:32,093 --> 00:20:34,178
How could I put on that junk?

243
00:20:36,158 --> 00:20:40,458
None of this would've happened
if you'd taken the blouse in yourself.

244
00:20:46,765 --> 00:20:50,098
- Han Gyu Yeong.
- What?

245
00:20:51,423 --> 00:20:53,523
There's something I want to ask.

246
00:20:53,991 --> 00:20:59,291
Why do you get to live the way you do,
while I have to live like this?

247
00:21:00,624 --> 00:21:02,251
What?

248
00:21:02,725 --> 00:21:07,205
You get to do everything you want,
so why do I...

249
00:21:08,225 --> 00:21:10,903
never get to do a single thing I want?

250
00:21:12,725 --> 00:21:16,121
- You're the firstborn.
- Only a year older?

251
00:21:16,633 --> 00:21:21,200
And you started school early,
so we've been in the same grade since.

252
00:21:21,304 --> 00:21:26,470
You're kind. Always yielding, selfless,
and overflowing with compassion.

253
00:21:26,730 --> 00:21:31,564
What if I start living
like you from now on?

254
00:21:31,785 --> 00:21:36,185
Enough. As Gyu Min says, you're Cinderella
and I'm the stepsister.

255
00:21:36,291 --> 00:21:38,447
We're just playing our parts.

256
00:21:38,725 --> 00:21:41,091
It's in your DNA. You were born that way.

257
00:21:41,364 --> 00:21:43,489
Nobody's born anything.

258
00:21:43,958 --> 00:21:45,625
It's because you won't do it.

259
00:21:45,925 --> 00:21:48,025
Because there's no one else.

260
00:21:48,325 --> 00:21:53,991
If I stopped too, this whole house
would fall apart. I have no choice.

261
00:21:54,391 --> 00:21:58,458
And I'm not kind. I'm selfish too.

262
00:21:58,591 --> 00:22:02,591
I want nice clothes and good food,

263
00:22:02,591 --> 00:22:06,258
I want to study, to go out
with my friends,

264
00:22:06,258 --> 00:22:07,870
I want someone good...

265
00:22:10,225 --> 00:22:15,391
Fine. Forget the blouse.
Easy now. We good?

266
00:22:16,418 --> 00:22:20,593
Watch out, kids. Bruce Banner
is about to turn into the Hulk!

267
00:22:39,925 --> 00:22:44,700
And my mom would welcome
whoever I brought home.

268
00:22:44,725 --> 00:22:46,991
But your mother wouldn't.

269
00:22:47,084 --> 00:22:50,151
Honestly, what her parents do,

270
00:22:50,176 --> 00:22:54,176
where she went to school, her job,
what her siblings do,

271
00:22:54,458 --> 00:22:56,391
isn't it normal for the chairwoman
to weigh all that?

272
00:22:56,558 --> 00:22:57,835
Don't you see that?

273
00:23:10,877 --> 00:23:12,010
Come in.

274
00:23:14,552 --> 00:23:16,718
You're still up?

275
00:23:17,838 --> 00:23:19,438
I couldn't sleep.

276
00:23:19,931 --> 00:23:22,497
Why not? Aren't you tired?

277
00:23:24,285 --> 00:23:25,918
There's a woman I like.

278
00:23:28,191 --> 00:23:29,958
Is that so?

279
00:23:30,291 --> 00:23:34,191
I told her how I feel,
and she turned me down.

280
00:23:35,358 --> 00:23:41,070
Who is this girl, so remarkable
that she'd dare turn down my son?

281
00:23:41,991 --> 00:23:45,825
But I'm not giving up.

282
00:23:46,478 --> 00:23:47,745
You said she turned you down.

283
00:23:48,138 --> 00:23:51,338
That's her business. I'm not giving up.

284
00:23:52,245 --> 00:23:56,645
All right. Good spirit, but...

285
00:23:58,557 --> 00:24:02,023
do you realize this is the first time
you've told me about a woman?

286
00:24:02,971 --> 00:24:04,191
I know.

287
00:24:06,058 --> 00:24:09,758
Thanks for telling me. I mean it, but...

288
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:18,910
The reason I'm telling you this...

289
00:24:21,291 --> 00:24:23,425
is that I need your help.

290
00:24:23,898 --> 00:24:26,298
My help? With what?

291
00:24:27,025 --> 00:24:31,222
Help me not give up on her.

292
00:24:34,525 --> 00:24:40,244
If you just support me,
I won't give her up, no matter what.

293
00:24:43,491 --> 00:24:46,391
- Mu Jin.
- I'll keep you posted.

294
00:24:46,391 --> 00:24:47,930
Good night.

295
00:24:56,111 --> 00:24:58,256
That boy...

296
00:25:36,518 --> 00:25:41,018
You may think I'm pathetic,
but I'll confess ten more times.

297
00:25:41,511 --> 00:25:45,352
Turn me down nine times,
and say yes just once.

298
00:25:52,925 --> 00:25:58,028
Good night, Gyu Rim.
See you tomorrow. Very gladly.

299
00:26:23,958 --> 00:26:25,662
You're the firstborn. You're kind.

300
00:26:26,158 --> 00:26:31,219
Always yielding, selfless,
and overflowing with compassion.

301
00:26:36,031 --> 00:26:38,864
As Gyu Min says, you're Cinderella
and I'm the stepsister.

302
00:26:38,991 --> 00:26:41,342
We're just playing our parts.

303
00:26:41,770 --> 00:26:44,169
It's in your DNA. You were born that way.

304
00:27:10,943 --> 00:27:13,177
You scared me. Ever heard of knocking?

305
00:27:13,561 --> 00:27:16,434
Do you know how to run the washer?
How to wash bedding?

306
00:27:16,575 --> 00:27:18,784
Do you know how to make radish kimchi?

307
00:27:19,276 --> 00:27:20,576
What are you on about?

308
00:27:21,861 --> 00:27:25,033
Gyu O is allergic to cucumber,
and Gyu Seo won't eat carrots.

309
00:27:25,058 --> 00:27:26,925
Gyu Min needs a bedtime story.

310
00:27:26,991 --> 00:27:28,725
Excuse me, Han Gyu Rim.

311
00:27:28,891 --> 00:27:31,266
Why are you suddenly telling me all this?

312
00:27:31,291 --> 00:27:32,891
Because you're doing it from now on.

313
00:27:32,991 --> 00:27:35,058
Look it up online if you don't know.

314
00:27:35,091 --> 00:27:38,658
You're smart. You'll pick it up faster
than someone dim like me.

315
00:27:38,658 --> 00:27:39,758
And what about you?

316
00:27:39,891 --> 00:27:41,058
Are you going somewhere?

317
00:27:42,458 --> 00:27:44,091
I asked where you're going.

318
00:27:44,602 --> 00:27:46,609
- Yeah.
- Where are you going?

319
00:27:47,225 --> 00:27:50,258
I'm getting married.

320
00:27:51,448 --> 00:27:52,658
What?

321
00:27:55,157 --> 00:27:58,591
- You're what? Getting married?
- That's right.

322
00:27:59,272 --> 00:28:01,684
Say something that makes sense.

323
00:28:01,816 --> 00:28:04,815
If you're going to lie, make it believable
so I can pretend to buy it.

324
00:28:05,091 --> 00:28:08,100
I know you haven't properly dated
since you graduated high school.

325
00:28:08,125 --> 00:28:10,391
What talent of yours lands a marriage?

326
00:28:10,658 --> 00:28:13,387
Marriage isn't about talent.
You love each other, so you marry.

327
00:28:13,412 --> 00:28:16,935
When did you ever have time
to date or fall in love?

328
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:18,559
Falling for someone takes ten seconds,

329
00:28:18,583 --> 00:28:21,400
and I may not date at leisure,
running around like you,

330
00:28:21,425 --> 00:28:25,398
but working together, clocking in and out
together, we did it hard. What of it?

331
00:28:27,458 --> 00:28:29,925
All right, fine. Let's say that's true.

332
00:28:30,625 --> 00:28:33,058
Then show me. The man you're marrying.

333
00:28:33,151 --> 00:28:35,384
- What?
- Why?

334
00:28:35,625 --> 00:28:39,458
My sister's getting married. Shouldn't
the sister-in-law meet the groom?

335
00:28:39,567 --> 00:28:41,900
You'll see him at the wedding.

336
00:28:41,925 --> 00:28:44,025
Bring him to me before the week's out.

337
00:28:44,125 --> 00:28:45,525
Then I'll believe you.

338
00:28:45,525 --> 00:28:47,058
He's very busy.

339
00:28:47,191 --> 00:28:48,358
There it is!

340
00:28:48,525 --> 00:28:53,383
If you're going to lie, use your head
and make it a little convincing.

341
00:28:58,304 --> 00:29:01,604
Best joke Han Gyu Rim's ever told.

342
00:29:02,625 --> 00:29:04,484
This Saturday.

343
00:29:05,331 --> 00:29:08,065
You'll meet him this Saturday.

344
00:29:09,171 --> 00:29:11,671
Got it? You'd better show up,
or you're dead.

345
00:29:24,891 --> 00:29:26,831
I'm out of my mind.

346
00:29:27,337 --> 00:29:30,495
What did I just do,
all to win against Han Gyu Yeong?

347
00:29:30,898 --> 00:29:35,698
What do I do? Seriously.

348
00:29:42,378 --> 00:29:43,747
Hey, Han Gyu O.

349
00:29:44,239 --> 00:29:46,784
Did you know Gyu Rim's getting married?

350
00:29:47,091 --> 00:29:48,614
Hey, twins!

351
00:29:49,565 --> 00:29:54,438
Gyu Rim's ditching you two to get married.
What will you do now?

352
00:30:04,491 --> 00:30:10,251
- Gyu Rim.
- Is what Gyu Yeong said true?

353
00:30:11,308 --> 00:30:13,688
No, I mean, the thing is...

354
00:30:13,814 --> 00:30:15,407
Are you really getting married?

355
00:30:16,975 --> 00:30:21,021
They're about to cry.
Just come clean before they do.

356
00:30:22,674 --> 00:30:24,004
Right,

357
00:30:24,178 --> 00:30:27,065
when you told me to hurry home
because you had something to say,

358
00:30:27,186 --> 00:30:28,988
was it about getting married?

359
00:30:29,532 --> 00:30:32,154
It's not that...

360
00:30:35,257 --> 00:30:36,301
I mean, yes.

361
00:30:36,955 --> 00:30:38,154
Out of nowhere?

362
00:30:38,695 --> 00:30:40,328
Without any warning?

363
00:30:41,708 --> 00:30:44,768
Who gets married at 24 these days?

364
00:30:44,828 --> 00:30:47,734
Why not? People do.

365
00:30:48,635 --> 00:30:50,415
Why are you looking at me like that?

366
00:30:51,428 --> 00:30:53,777
Frankly, I'm not your mother,

367
00:30:54,392 --> 00:30:57,630
so should I cook, do laundry,
wash dishes, and vacuum for you,

368
00:30:57,638 --> 00:31:00,694
then work shifts outside,
for the rest of my life?

369
00:31:00,701 --> 00:31:01,915
Without ever marrying?

370
00:31:02,195 --> 00:31:04,515
That's not what I meant.

371
00:31:06,875 --> 00:31:12,981
Don't go, Gyu Rim.

372
00:31:13,321 --> 00:31:14,334
Don't worry.

373
00:31:14,362 --> 00:31:17,154
Even without me,
Gyu Yeong will take good care of you.

374
00:31:19,213 --> 00:31:20,287
Me?

375
00:31:38,047 --> 00:31:39,826
What am I supposed to do?

376
00:31:43,408 --> 00:31:45,655
Han Gyu Rim's got nerve.

377
00:31:45,687 --> 00:31:47,800
- Now you've made them cry.
- What do you mean?

378
00:31:47,868 --> 00:31:50,154
I thought you'd admit it was a lie
once they started crying?

379
00:31:50,321 --> 00:31:51,900
It's not a lie, I swear.

380
00:31:52,094 --> 00:31:54,361
Fine. Saturday will tell.

381
00:31:54,501 --> 00:31:58,041
Suddenly I can't wait for Saturday.

382
00:32:15,135 --> 00:32:17,155
I should've said I was enlisting.

383
00:32:17,701 --> 00:32:19,575
That's how dim I am,

384
00:32:19,601 --> 00:32:21,115
which is why nobody respects me.

385
00:32:23,881 --> 00:32:25,128
Why are you hitting your head?

386
00:32:43,654 --> 00:32:45,315
About the text I sent last night,

387
00:32:47,995 --> 00:32:50,328
I'd had a bit to drink.

388
00:32:51,794 --> 00:32:54,128
It's fine. You don't have to apologize.

389
00:32:54,248 --> 00:32:55,954
Drunk words, sober truth.

390
00:32:59,694 --> 00:33:02,764
If I came on too fast,

391
00:33:03,659 --> 00:33:09,122
and caught you off guard, I'll slow down.

392
00:33:11,494 --> 00:33:13,148
So you don't get dizzy.

393
00:33:13,727 --> 00:33:16,830
When I help you and look out for you,

394
00:33:17,097 --> 00:33:19,934
or even get a little carried away,

395
00:33:22,174 --> 00:33:23,451
just think of it,

396
00:33:25,868 --> 00:33:27,554
as coworker loyalty. Nothing more.

397
00:33:31,941 --> 00:33:33,593
In return,

398
00:33:35,034 --> 00:33:36,941
just keep your heart fluttering for me.

399
00:33:37,855 --> 00:33:39,395
Hide it if you like,

400
00:33:41,201 --> 00:33:42,548
but I'd rather you didn't.

401
00:34:06,116 --> 00:34:08,212
(Gyu Yeong)

402
00:34:13,247 --> 00:34:14,258
Hello.

403
00:34:15,113 --> 00:34:17,187
That guy sitting next to you,

404
00:34:17,303 --> 00:34:19,326
is he the one you're marrying?

405
00:34:26,447 --> 00:34:27,510
Yes.

406
00:34:27,971 --> 00:34:29,001
Liar.

407
00:34:42,347 --> 00:34:45,400
It's not a lie. I'm busy. Bye.

408
00:34:51,894 --> 00:34:54,221
Did you just brush lint off my shirt?

409
00:34:56,128 --> 00:34:57,128
Yes.

410
00:35:13,661 --> 00:35:16,107
Really? Your sister's really marrying?

411
00:35:17,027 --> 00:35:19,006
You actually believe that?

412
00:35:19,520 --> 00:35:20,534
It's not true?

413
00:35:20,948 --> 00:35:23,634
How are you even a TA
with that little common sense?

414
00:35:24,841 --> 00:35:26,623
If someone says you have a pure aura,

415
00:35:26,651 --> 00:35:27,779
asks if you're into spiritual stuff,

416
00:35:27,800 --> 00:35:29,810
or tells you to come to a ritual,

417
00:35:30,104 --> 00:35:32,148
run and don't look back.

418
00:35:32,936 --> 00:35:34,708
Believe what's believable.

419
00:35:34,733 --> 00:35:37,666
Han Gyu Rim's just worn out,
so she put on that ridiculous show...

420
00:35:40,735 --> 00:35:42,574
Wait, then who was that man?

421
00:35:42,702 --> 00:35:43,721
What man?

422
00:35:43,741 --> 00:35:46,074
It did smell hastily arranged.

423
00:35:47,113 --> 00:35:49,693
But even from far off,
the guy was seriously handsome.

424
00:35:49,928 --> 00:35:51,092
I'm telling you.

425
00:35:51,186 --> 00:35:54,220
My friend was at that hotel for lunch
and saw the whole thing.

426
00:35:54,441 --> 00:35:57,041
Han Gyu Yeong got caught
playing her gold-digger act.

427
00:35:57,334 --> 00:35:58,443
Honestly,

428
00:35:58,868 --> 00:36:00,923
just hearing it is secondhand shame.

429
00:36:01,044 --> 00:36:02,481
Doesn't she know what shame is?

430
00:36:02,501 --> 00:36:04,448
How could she?

431
00:36:04,768 --> 00:36:07,181
Why do you think
they call her the Draft Board?

432
00:36:07,321 --> 00:36:11,008
A truckload of guys enlisted, took leave,
or dropped out because of her.

433
00:36:11,920 --> 00:36:14,267
Can't she last a day without a man?

434
00:36:14,873 --> 00:36:17,951
A disgrace to women, med school,
and this university.

435
00:36:25,141 --> 00:36:26,150
Sorry.

436
00:36:26,272 --> 00:36:29,160
It reeked so badly in here,
I thought this was the trash can.

437
00:36:29,488 --> 00:36:30,715
You've got to be kidding.

438
00:36:30,834 --> 00:36:32,439
Are you two out of your minds?

439
00:36:33,167 --> 00:36:34,748
Are you okay?

440
00:36:37,950 --> 00:36:38,962
Hey!

441
00:36:38,987 --> 00:36:42,381
Are you insane? Seong Ju, you okay?

442
00:36:43,988 --> 00:36:46,831
I know you've liked Shin Jeong Rok
since freshman year,

443
00:36:46,892 --> 00:36:49,289
that you confessed and got shot down,

444
00:36:49,376 --> 00:36:52,159
and you're so bitter he's dating me,

445
00:36:53,188 --> 00:36:54,581
so don't push it.

446
00:36:55,195 --> 00:36:57,004
Who's to blame that you don't measure up?

447
00:36:57,029 --> 00:36:58,151
Are you okay?

448
00:36:58,900 --> 00:37:01,131
Be her lapdog if you want,

449
00:37:01,272 --> 00:37:03,614
but it's getting pathetic,
so tone it down.

450
00:37:08,628 --> 00:37:10,461
Is she out of her mind?

451
00:37:11,328 --> 00:37:12,347
You okay?

452
00:37:19,668 --> 00:37:21,295
She's insane, isn't she?

453
00:37:28,941 --> 00:37:31,064
This is bad.

454
00:37:31,837 --> 00:37:33,648
So annoying.

455
00:37:38,274 --> 00:37:39,288
Honey.

456
00:37:39,501 --> 00:37:40,501
Where are you?

457
00:37:41,141 --> 00:37:42,494
I stopped by the university,

458
00:37:42,501 --> 00:37:44,695
to see Chancellor Kim. And you?

459
00:37:44,928 --> 00:37:47,915
Seo Hyeon's working late,
so I'm bringing her a lunchbox.

460
00:37:48,928 --> 00:37:51,261
You'll head back to the office, right?

461
00:37:51,368 --> 00:37:53,892
I'll see after meeting Chancellor Kim.

462
00:37:55,388 --> 00:37:56,771
Hello?

463
00:37:56,952 --> 00:38:00,484
Honey?

464
00:38:01,054 --> 00:38:02,335
What's wrong?

465
00:38:02,688 --> 00:38:03,862
Were you in an accident?

466
00:38:04,187 --> 00:38:05,705
No.

467
00:38:05,819 --> 00:38:07,274
I was just careless.

468
00:38:07,328 --> 00:38:08,869
Are you hurt?

469
00:38:09,489 --> 00:38:10,500
Hello?

470
00:38:10,947 --> 00:38:13,100
I'm fine. I'm not hurt.

471
00:38:13,554 --> 00:38:14,984
Where are you?

472
00:38:15,292 --> 00:38:18,001
- Honey.
- This is unbelievable.

473
00:38:18,026 --> 00:38:19,052
You're not hurt, are you?

474
00:38:19,146 --> 00:38:21,553
- I'll call my insurer and handle it.
- What are you doing?

475
00:38:21,578 --> 00:38:22,655
Don't worry too much.

476
00:38:22,657 --> 00:38:25,841
Who slams on the brakes at a yellow light?

477
00:38:25,866 --> 00:38:27,465
Roll down your window.

478
00:38:28,455 --> 00:38:29,821
Hello?

479
00:38:34,274 --> 00:38:35,535
- Honey?
- Honey.

480
00:38:37,901 --> 00:38:39,248
Roll your window down.

481
00:38:39,774 --> 00:38:41,641
I'll call you back.

482
00:38:41,666 --> 00:38:42,666
All right.

483
00:38:47,528 --> 00:38:49,941
It was just a minor fender bender.

484
00:38:51,414 --> 00:38:53,468
Yes, I called the insurer right away.

485
00:38:55,915 --> 00:38:58,875
I'm not hurt. I'm perfectly fine.

486
00:39:01,687 --> 00:39:02,860
All right.

487
00:39:03,049 --> 00:39:06,152
I'll get checked head to toe,

488
00:39:06,485 --> 00:39:08,910
and prove there's nothing wrong with me.

489
00:39:08,964 --> 00:39:10,218
Happy now?

490
00:39:11,368 --> 00:39:14,468
Yes. See you at home, honey.

491
00:39:18,393 --> 00:39:19,470
Honey?

492
00:39:20,665 --> 00:39:22,288
You remarried already?

493
00:39:22,421 --> 00:39:24,844
Whether I marry twice or three times,

494
00:39:25,092 --> 00:39:26,981
what business is it of yours?

495
00:39:32,241 --> 00:39:33,354
Why the disrespect?

496
00:39:33,595 --> 00:39:34,622
Why not?

497
00:39:35,290 --> 00:39:37,354
I was the wife who bore three children,

498
00:39:37,915 --> 00:39:41,215
and you threw me out overnight
for another woman. To scum like you,

499
00:39:41,296 --> 00:39:43,068
do I owe respect on top of that?

500
00:39:46,974 --> 00:39:48,328
Looks like you married well.

501
00:39:48,415 --> 00:39:49,626
From what I saw,

502
00:39:50,600 --> 00:39:52,541
you're driving a nice car these days.

503
00:39:52,566 --> 00:39:53,597
Yes.

504
00:39:55,113 --> 00:39:56,749
As the kids say,

505
00:39:57,078 --> 00:39:59,575
junk car out, import in.

506
00:40:00,168 --> 00:40:01,488
Turns out it's true.

507
00:40:01,775 --> 00:40:02,861
Are you doing well?

508
00:40:03,695 --> 00:40:06,375
I'm not actually curious,
so you don't have to answer.

509
00:40:06,601 --> 00:40:08,208
Don't you miss the kids?

510
00:40:09,008 --> 00:40:11,974
Living this well,
how could you not call even once?

511
00:40:12,074 --> 00:40:13,975
If I tell Gyu Rim, Gyu O, and Gyu Yeong,

512
00:40:14,674 --> 00:40:16,219
that I ran into you,

513
00:40:16,428 --> 00:40:19,735
and you're living disgustingly well,
what do you think they'd say?

514
00:40:19,760 --> 00:40:21,929
And whose fault is all that?

515
00:40:22,608 --> 00:40:24,328
You made it this way.

516
00:40:24,540 --> 00:40:25,555
So what?

517
00:40:26,117 --> 00:40:27,655
Should I have left the woman I loved?

518
00:40:27,955 --> 00:40:29,415
I was all she had.

519
00:40:29,486 --> 00:40:32,240
Brand the mother of my child
an adulteress?

520
00:40:34,873 --> 00:40:39,495
Right. What a tearjerker of a romance.

521
00:40:40,001 --> 00:40:41,667
If only it weren't mine.

522
00:40:43,155 --> 00:40:44,394
What did you do to your face?

523
00:40:45,595 --> 00:40:47,109
You look younger and prettier,

524
00:40:48,249 --> 00:40:50,287
than when we split. How?

525
00:40:52,167 --> 00:40:53,698
Shut your mouth,

526
00:40:53,997 --> 00:40:58,455
and tell your wife this. If I hear
even a whisper she's mistreating my kids,

527
00:40:58,704 --> 00:41:00,614
I'll come and kill her.

528
00:41:04,901 --> 00:41:06,191
She's gone.

529
00:41:06,799 --> 00:41:08,019
She ran off years ago.

530
00:41:08,044 --> 00:41:09,139
Left the twins behind.

531
00:41:11,260 --> 00:41:12,261
Why?

532
00:41:13,170 --> 00:41:14,681
Did you cheat again?

533
00:41:14,975 --> 00:41:17,475
I didn't. She did.

534
00:41:17,963 --> 00:41:20,428
You know that accounting manager?

535
00:41:20,468 --> 00:41:22,074
Tall as a beanpole,

536
00:41:22,209 --> 00:41:24,375
bald as an egg. With him.

537
00:41:25,067 --> 00:41:26,570
Then what about the kids?

538
00:41:27,189 --> 00:41:31,401
How long have they been living
with no mother?

539
00:41:32,555 --> 00:41:33,651
A while now.

540
00:41:33,676 --> 00:41:35,793
About six years?

541
00:41:36,840 --> 00:41:39,943
So to find a mother for those poor kids,

542
00:41:40,116 --> 00:41:41,988
I'm still out there looking,

543
00:41:44,289 --> 00:41:47,928
but no woman comes close
to their real mother.

544
00:41:48,716 --> 00:41:51,076
Listen, forget all this.

545
00:41:51,351 --> 00:41:53,061
Want to see the kids?

546
00:41:56,455 --> 00:41:58,028
Come on, let's go.

547
00:41:58,121 --> 00:41:59,590
I'll get this to go,

548
00:41:59,615 --> 00:42:04,081
and once you see the children you bore,
you'll feel differently.

549
00:42:04,875 --> 00:42:06,432
Get out of my way,

550
00:42:06,839 --> 00:42:09,820
and if we ever cross paths again,
don't you dare acknowledge me.

551
00:42:10,480 --> 00:42:13,194
I was wrong, honey.

552
00:42:14,420 --> 00:42:15,874
Having lived a bit,

553
00:42:15,899 --> 00:42:18,034
no woman compares to you.

554
00:42:18,414 --> 00:42:20,628
I got what I deserved.

555
00:42:21,474 --> 00:42:23,694
I'm so sorry, honey. Truly sorry.

556
00:42:26,227 --> 00:42:28,404
Come back to me, Gyu Rim's mother.

557
00:42:29,141 --> 00:42:31,404
For the sake of those poor kids, please.

558
00:42:31,429 --> 00:42:33,151
Hate me, but give me one more chance.

559
00:42:33,894 --> 00:42:36,680
- Honey, just one more chance...
- Let go of me, you creep!

560
00:42:51,295 --> 00:42:53,075
What's wrong? Are you sick?

561
00:42:53,615 --> 00:42:56,108
The tofu I had at lunch
must have gone bad.

562
00:42:57,715 --> 00:42:59,161
My stomach's rumbling again.

563
00:42:59,208 --> 00:43:00,655
There's nothing left in me.

564
00:43:03,161 --> 00:43:05,581
Are you like this around Mu Jin too?

565
00:43:06,355 --> 00:43:08,463
Do you tell him everything
going on inside you,

566
00:43:08,517 --> 00:43:09,655
with zero filter?

567
00:43:09,668 --> 00:43:10,672
Are you crazy?

568
00:43:10,687 --> 00:43:12,921
If I marry Mu Jin,
I'll never even fart in front of him.

569
00:43:12,961 --> 00:43:14,801
Marriage, my foot.

570
00:43:14,967 --> 00:43:16,767
He ignores your texts and emails.

571
00:43:17,188 --> 00:43:18,955
Didn't he flat out reject you?

572
00:43:18,961 --> 00:43:21,521
I haven't been officially rejected.

573
00:43:24,446 --> 00:43:27,048
Right. Too early to despair.

574
00:43:28,167 --> 00:43:29,708
Which brings me to this, Seo Hyeon.

575
00:43:30,315 --> 00:43:31,701
Let's form an alliance.

576
00:43:31,726 --> 00:43:32,738
An alliance?

577
00:43:33,401 --> 00:43:34,407
What kind?

578
00:43:34,988 --> 00:43:37,537
I'm not sure how to explain this,

579
00:43:37,698 --> 00:43:40,493
but you, me, Mu Jin, and Han Gyu Rim,

580
00:43:41,316 --> 00:43:43,293
are all tangled up in a tricky knot.

581
00:43:43,318 --> 00:43:46,143
Han Gyu Rim? Who is...

582
00:43:48,208 --> 00:43:50,268
Han Gyu Rim is who Mu Jin likes, right?

583
00:43:51,694 --> 00:43:53,744
You're a psychic when it comes to him.

584
00:43:53,752 --> 00:43:54,848
Truly gifted.

585
00:43:55,127 --> 00:43:56,888
Anyway, the point is,

586
00:43:59,054 --> 00:44:00,594
I like Han Gyu Rim too.

587
00:44:03,148 --> 00:44:04,488
What's so special about her?

588
00:44:05,036 --> 00:44:06,515
Is she really that amazing?

589
00:44:07,601 --> 00:44:10,855
It's not that she's amazing.
She's just impossible to resist.

590
00:44:10,948 --> 00:44:12,594
Kind, cute, and pretty on top of it.

591
00:44:12,596 --> 00:44:13,601
How is that fair?

592
00:44:13,628 --> 00:44:14,976
Anyway,

593
00:44:15,163 --> 00:44:18,521
this is the first time
Mu Jin and I have wanted the same person.

594
00:44:18,754 --> 00:44:20,892
You want Mu Jin,

595
00:44:21,013 --> 00:44:22,865
and I want Han Gyu Rim.

596
00:44:23,139 --> 00:44:24,716
If things work out for you two,

597
00:44:24,844 --> 00:44:26,701
my odds with Han Gyu Rim go way up.

598
00:44:27,408 --> 00:44:29,408
So, an alliance?

599
00:44:29,884 --> 00:44:33,821
I'll do everything I can to get
you and Mu Jin together.

600
00:44:34,334 --> 00:44:37,011
So you pull out every trick you know,

601
00:44:37,035 --> 00:44:39,194
and turn me into an irresistible man.

602
00:44:39,235 --> 00:44:41,055
So Han Gyu Rim falls hard for me.

603
00:44:41,095 --> 00:44:43,068
Who on earth is this Han Gyu Rim?

604
00:44:43,335 --> 00:44:44,742
What's so great about her,

605
00:44:44,767 --> 00:44:47,712
that Kim Mu Jin and Park Jeong Woo
both lost their minds at once?

606
00:45:18,228 --> 00:45:20,148
Han Gyu O is totally screwed.

607
00:45:20,815 --> 00:45:22,775
So he can't come to school for ten days?

608
00:45:23,155 --> 00:45:24,281
With that suspension,

609
00:45:24,408 --> 00:45:25,761
he can't compete either.

610
00:45:25,915 --> 00:45:27,549
Sports college is off the table, right?

611
00:45:29,290 --> 00:45:30,428
What a shame.

612
00:46:21,421 --> 00:46:23,400
You jerk.

613
00:46:23,975 --> 00:46:27,154
How can love just change?

614
00:46:29,368 --> 00:46:30,381
Excuse me?

615
00:46:32,934 --> 00:46:34,480
Could you go cry somewhere else?

616
00:46:36,627 --> 00:46:39,300
Hey, does this place belong to you?

617
00:46:39,834 --> 00:46:41,620
This is where he and I...

618
00:46:43,822 --> 00:46:44,934
No!

619
00:46:45,388 --> 00:46:50,334
I dropped my phone. My phone!

620
00:46:50,375 --> 00:46:52,881
That's dangerous! Are you trying to die?

621
00:46:52,915 --> 00:46:55,988
What if he calls? My phone!

622
00:46:57,008 --> 00:46:58,751
I'll go get it,

623
00:46:59,058 --> 00:47:01,175
so don't do anything stupid. Stay put.

624
00:47:02,338 --> 00:47:04,814
- My phone.
- Answer me.

625
00:47:07,494 --> 00:47:08,494
Okay.

626
00:47:18,308 --> 00:47:19,815
Just a little more.

627
00:47:29,765 --> 00:47:35,828
It still turns on? Why is it fine?

628
00:47:39,915 --> 00:47:40,915
Hey!

629
00:47:44,755 --> 00:47:49,008
Just for a few hours,

630
00:47:49,202 --> 00:47:51,791
or even one hour is fine,

631
00:47:51,892 --> 00:47:53,695
could you hold on to this for me?

632
00:47:53,988 --> 00:47:54,988
Why would I?

633
00:47:55,661 --> 00:47:58,414
Because I'll break down
and call that jerk.

634
00:47:58,844 --> 00:48:00,637
Crying, begging,

635
00:48:00,829 --> 00:48:03,260
making a complete fool of myself.

636
00:48:03,648 --> 00:48:04,741
A hundred dollars.

637
00:48:08,241 --> 00:48:10,381
I'll pay you 100 dollars an hour.

638
00:48:10,908 --> 00:48:12,851
One hour, 100 dollars.

639
00:48:12,978 --> 00:48:14,841
Two hours, 200 dollars.

640
00:48:15,014 --> 00:48:19,987
No, factoring in all the scenes
I'm going to make,

641
00:48:20,168 --> 00:48:22,448
I'll make it 300 dollars.

642
00:48:23,794 --> 00:48:25,753
You know what shifts pay these days.

643
00:48:25,975 --> 00:48:28,155
This is seriously good money.

644
00:48:29,567 --> 00:48:30,567
Deal.

645
00:48:32,608 --> 00:48:34,395
Just don't take it back later.

646
00:48:35,674 --> 00:48:38,720
Okay. Thank you.

647
00:48:52,881 --> 00:48:53,921
Welcome.

648
00:48:57,775 --> 00:48:59,135
Please sit wherever you like.

649
00:48:59,142 --> 00:49:00,208
Would you like this table?

650
00:49:00,235 --> 00:49:01,241
Yes.

651
00:49:07,755 --> 00:49:09,701
Hello. Here's the menu.

652
00:49:09,726 --> 00:49:11,332
Take your time and order when ready.

653
00:49:11,357 --> 00:49:12,924
I'll bring water shortly.

654
00:49:15,907 --> 00:49:18,594
Will anyone be joining you?

655
00:49:19,682 --> 00:49:21,017
I'm looking for Gyu Rim.

656
00:49:21,091 --> 00:49:23,668
Han Gyu Rim, that is.

657
00:49:24,115 --> 00:49:25,501
May I ask why?

658
00:49:26,194 --> 00:49:27,643
That's none of your concern.

659
00:49:27,811 --> 00:49:29,828
Just fetch the girl for me.

660
00:49:30,675 --> 00:49:33,464
She's stepped out for a moment...

661
00:49:34,181 --> 00:49:36,095
Then when will she be back?

662
00:49:36,481 --> 00:49:39,487
I have to see her today.

663
00:49:39,794 --> 00:49:42,694
I owe her a debt to repay.

664
00:49:42,774 --> 00:49:43,774
A debt?

665
00:49:46,828 --> 00:49:48,715
Sir, please open the door.

666
00:49:53,261 --> 00:49:56,807
Ma'am, are you all right? Ma'am?

667
00:49:57,478 --> 00:50:01,931
Are you the lady Gyu Rim helped
not long ago?

668
00:50:02,079 --> 00:50:04,028
- At the bus stop.
- That's right.

669
00:50:04,992 --> 00:50:06,981
So the girl told you about it.

670
00:50:06,983 --> 00:50:09,048
No, I was there that day too.

671
00:50:09,341 --> 00:50:11,115
You probably don't remember me...

672
00:50:12,092 --> 00:50:14,712
You were there that day too?

673
00:50:14,737 --> 00:50:15,780
Yes.

674
00:50:16,241 --> 00:50:18,629
Gyu Rim and I were on the bus
about to leave,

675
00:50:18,631 --> 00:50:20,328
when you collapsed.

676
00:50:21,115 --> 00:50:22,127
What?

677
00:50:22,375 --> 00:50:23,433
So you're telling me,

678
00:50:24,174 --> 00:50:28,395
you saw someone collapse and just left?

679
00:50:29,188 --> 00:50:30,744
I didn't leave. The bus did.

680
00:50:30,769 --> 00:50:31,917
Enough.

681
00:50:32,841 --> 00:50:37,501
What would blaming you now change?

682
00:50:38,101 --> 00:50:42,674
You're hardly the only one these days
lower than a beast.

683
00:50:43,914 --> 00:50:45,042
Come to think of it,

684
00:50:45,990 --> 00:50:49,348
a girl like Gyu Rim is a rare species.

685
00:50:49,375 --> 00:50:51,635
A natural treasure.

686
00:50:52,405 --> 00:50:55,235
You wretched thing.

687
00:50:55,268 --> 00:50:57,470
No blood, no tears in you.

688
00:51:00,454 --> 00:51:02,361
I'll bring your water shortly.

689
00:51:09,935 --> 00:51:12,154
Is that brave or just stupid?

690
00:51:27,907 --> 00:51:31,677
- I mean it.
- I want something to drink...

691
00:51:33,902 --> 00:51:35,168
Is that Yeon Su?

692
00:51:35,429 --> 00:51:36,557
What do I do?

693
00:51:36,912 --> 00:51:38,054
What now?

694
00:51:39,695 --> 00:51:40,701
Okay.

695
00:51:40,728 --> 00:51:41,749
In that case,

696
00:51:41,864 --> 00:51:44,835
- Grab me something cold to drink.
- Sure, I'll go get it.

697
00:51:56,394 --> 00:51:57,611
I thought,

698
00:51:58,475 --> 00:51:59,841
she was someone I knew...

699
00:52:11,181 --> 00:52:12,634
You don't want to run into him, right?

700
00:52:15,088 --> 00:52:18,781
On three, we stand up.
Just look ahead and walk.

701
00:52:19,121 --> 00:52:21,808
One, two, three.

702
00:52:51,561 --> 00:52:52,761
Today,

703
00:52:53,258 --> 00:52:55,128
thank you for everything.

704
00:52:56,968 --> 00:52:59,135
Sure. Take care.

705
00:53:09,188 --> 00:53:10,214
A hundred dollars!

706
00:53:11,748 --> 00:53:12,814
Hey!

707
00:53:13,408 --> 00:53:14,452
Excuse me!

708
00:53:15,980 --> 00:53:17,528
Hey, my pay!

709
00:53:29,128 --> 00:53:30,708
- We meet again.
- Yes.

710
00:53:30,766 --> 00:53:34,180
I'm not here for you today.
I'm here to take my mom home.

711
00:53:34,205 --> 00:53:35,391
To take your mother?

712
00:53:48,094 --> 00:53:49,541
How did you get here?

713
00:53:49,566 --> 00:53:50,893
Mom, let's go.

714
00:53:51,488 --> 00:53:54,714
- Hold on a minute.
- Let's go.

715
00:53:54,716 --> 00:53:56,095
Just wait.

716
00:53:56,321 --> 00:53:58,155
I said I have to see Gyu Rim.

717
00:53:58,541 --> 00:54:00,021
Hello, ma'am.

718
00:54:01,378 --> 00:54:03,340
There you are.

719
00:54:03,894 --> 00:54:06,741
It's so good to see you again.

720
00:54:07,148 --> 00:54:10,512
I'm so glad to see
you looking healthy again.

721
00:54:10,914 --> 00:54:12,786
But my son...

722
00:54:12,853 --> 00:54:14,514
kept insisting on repaying you,

723
00:54:14,515 --> 00:54:18,333
or at least buying you a meal.

724
00:54:18,393 --> 00:54:21,341
Why wouldn't you let him?

725
00:54:21,741 --> 00:54:25,028
I have to repay your kindness somehow.

726
00:54:25,560 --> 00:54:27,120
I'm really fine.

727
00:54:27,168 --> 00:54:29,634
Your good health is enough for me.

728
00:54:30,828 --> 00:54:32,141
What am I to do?

729
00:54:32,534 --> 00:54:35,239
You even say the loveliest things.

730
00:54:35,401 --> 00:54:38,559
How could I not adore you?

731
00:54:38,561 --> 00:54:40,941
All right, let's go home now.
You're going to...

732
00:54:40,966 --> 00:54:43,099
make her uncomfortable.

733
00:54:43,468 --> 00:54:47,754
My son dated a girl for over five years.

734
00:54:47,770 --> 00:54:50,534
- Why bring that up?
- Hush now.

735
00:54:50,568 --> 00:54:53,328
We adored her, truly,

736
00:54:54,301 --> 00:54:58,495
but the moment our finances turned,

737
00:54:58,650 --> 00:55:00,715
she showed her true colors.

738
00:55:01,048 --> 00:55:02,131
Turns out,

739
00:55:02,133 --> 00:55:03,770
no money, no connections,

740
00:55:03,772 --> 00:55:05,637
and nothing left to squeeze out of him,

741
00:55:05,864 --> 00:55:09,667
and she stops treating him like a person.
That wretched girl!

742
00:55:11,927 --> 00:55:13,601
That's the kind of woman she was.

743
00:55:13,888 --> 00:55:15,441
That's enough!

744
00:55:15,783 --> 00:55:17,033
- Let's go.
- That whole thing... Hey!

745
00:55:17,041 --> 00:55:18,541
- Let's go.
- Hey!

746
00:55:18,543 --> 00:55:19,672
- Let's go!
- You rotten brat!

747
00:55:19,674 --> 00:55:21,319
After going through that,

748
00:55:21,321 --> 00:55:23,095
my health took a bad turn.

749
00:55:23,621 --> 00:55:25,181
I'd just collapse,

750
00:55:25,182 --> 00:55:26,648
anywhere and everywhere.

751
00:55:27,053 --> 00:55:31,903
But seeing how kind and lovely you are,

752
00:55:33,001 --> 00:55:34,501
just lifts my spirits.

753
00:55:38,081 --> 00:55:39,100
Let's go.

754
00:55:40,528 --> 00:55:42,192
So here's what I'm thinking.

755
00:55:43,333 --> 00:55:47,253
Humor an old woman's wish,

756
00:55:47,601 --> 00:55:49,670
and meet my son just once.

757
00:55:50,518 --> 00:55:53,134
Actually, make that three.

758
00:55:54,821 --> 00:55:57,149
I'm not asking for anything.

759
00:55:57,283 --> 00:56:02,168
Just meet as friends, have a meal,
go on a few dates...

760
00:56:02,170 --> 00:56:04,228
Isn't that exactly what you're asking?

761
00:56:04,475 --> 00:56:05,501
Excuse me?

762
00:56:06,008 --> 00:56:09,682
I don't know how repaying a kindness
turned into granting your wish,

763
00:56:09,684 --> 00:56:10,960
but by your own account,

764
00:56:10,962 --> 00:56:12,866
Gyu Rim is the one who saved you.

765
00:56:12,868 --> 00:56:14,867
Why should the savior have to grant
wishes on top of that?

766
00:56:14,869 --> 00:56:16,221
I don't follow.

767
00:56:16,568 --> 00:56:19,528
Did I ask you to follow?

768
00:56:21,381 --> 00:56:23,227
No matter how I think about it,

769
00:56:23,252 --> 00:56:27,301
I'd regret losing this girl
for the rest of my life.

770
00:56:27,326 --> 00:56:31,252
Where else would I ever find
someone like you?

771
00:56:31,466 --> 00:56:32,481
What should I do?

772
00:56:32,575 --> 00:56:35,132
If you regret it, you regret it.
If you don't find her, you don't.

773
00:56:35,135 --> 00:56:37,186
Why keep pressuring her?

774
00:56:37,188 --> 00:56:39,128
Stay out of this.

775
00:56:41,653 --> 00:56:43,413
Mu Jin, go tend to your work.

776
00:56:44,082 --> 00:56:46,635
That's right, Kim Mu Jin.
Go to another table.

777
00:56:54,703 --> 00:56:59,406
And don't you go around
with a pretty boy like him.

778
00:56:59,431 --> 00:57:01,634
No. Don't go near him.

779
00:57:02,261 --> 00:57:04,366
He watched someone collapse,

780
00:57:04,368 --> 00:57:09,548
and breezed off because he was busy.
That's the brute he is.

781
00:57:10,128 --> 00:57:11,194
Is that so?

782
00:57:15,835 --> 00:57:17,015
- Let's go.
- Of all the...

783
00:57:17,017 --> 00:57:18,719
- Have you lost it today?
- Hey!

784
00:57:18,721 --> 00:57:21,068
- Just wait!
- Let's go!

785
00:57:21,070 --> 00:57:22,534
You rotten brat!

786
00:57:26,808 --> 00:57:28,028
Are you disappointed in me?

787
00:57:28,515 --> 00:57:29,534
No.

788
00:57:31,115 --> 00:57:32,721
Let him buy you a meal.

789
00:57:33,115 --> 00:57:34,841
Go on three dates with him.

790
00:57:35,735 --> 00:57:39,617
Pushing her own feelings and position
without listening to the other person,

791
00:57:39,642 --> 00:57:41,205
is a form of violence too.

792
00:57:44,741 --> 00:57:45,761
Why are you looking at me like that?

793
00:57:45,815 --> 00:57:47,167
It's just strange,

794
00:57:47,229 --> 00:57:49,861
hearing that from you, of all people.

795
00:57:54,361 --> 00:57:55,381
So,

796
00:57:56,870 --> 00:57:58,208
are you actually going to meet him?

797
00:57:59,181 --> 00:58:00,821
Do you grant every request?

798
00:58:00,915 --> 00:58:02,246
You never grant a single one of mine.

799
00:58:02,248 --> 00:58:04,319
When did I ever grant every request?

800
00:58:04,321 --> 00:58:07,246
You will, though.
Not after she pleaded like that.

801
00:58:07,248 --> 00:58:08,735
Your heart softens again.

802
00:58:10,235 --> 00:58:11,932
So, that man.

803
00:58:12,900 --> 00:58:15,635
Are you going to eat and date with him?

804
00:58:15,694 --> 00:58:18,107
He's hardly old enough
for you to call him that.

805
00:58:18,475 --> 00:58:20,123
Does that matter?

806
00:58:20,983 --> 00:58:22,425
That man, that guy,

807
00:58:23,240 --> 00:58:24,808
are you really going to meet him?

808
00:58:25,841 --> 00:58:26,841
No.

809
00:58:44,475 --> 00:58:45,484
Hello?

810
00:58:45,798 --> 00:58:47,827
Is this Han Gyu Rim?

811
00:58:48,122 --> 00:58:49,338
Yes, speaking.

812
00:58:49,752 --> 00:58:52,981
Hello, I'm with Buy Mart delivery.

813
00:58:53,215 --> 00:58:56,245
Han Gyu Yeong has sent you a washer
as a gift.

814
00:58:56,247 --> 00:58:58,434
When would you like it delivered?

815
00:58:58,641 --> 00:59:00,513
Han Gyu Yeong sent me what?

816
00:59:00,813 --> 00:59:01,957
A washing machine?

817
00:59:13,981 --> 00:59:15,320
Why are you here?

818
00:59:17,301 --> 00:59:18,756
You turned down the washer?

819
00:59:19,328 --> 00:59:21,121
Where did a washer even come from?

820
00:59:21,855 --> 00:59:25,521
That pathetic marriage act
was about the washer, wasn't it?

821
00:59:25,714 --> 00:59:29,564
I wondered why you'd suddenly act out
and what the problem was,

822
00:59:29,786 --> 00:59:31,634
and that washer really is ancient.

823
00:59:32,075 --> 00:59:35,114
- So I splurged on a gift.
- A washer is a gift?

824
00:59:35,855 --> 00:59:39,093
So you'll upgrade my equipment
and I should just keep doing laundry?

825
00:59:39,095 --> 00:59:41,948
- That's not exactly...
- Han Gyu Yeong.

826
00:59:42,861 --> 00:59:45,233
What do you actually think I am?

827
00:59:45,700 --> 00:59:46,800
Not a washer, then?

828
00:59:47,069 --> 00:59:48,076
What is it?

829
00:59:48,150 --> 00:59:49,892
- A vacuum and a dishwasher?
- Hey!

830
00:59:49,895 --> 00:59:51,339
Then what?

831
00:59:51,341 --> 00:59:54,128
Why are you suddenly
talking about getting married?

832
00:59:54,614 --> 00:59:55,724
If you go off and marry,

833
00:59:56,005 --> 00:59:57,148
what happens to the rest of us?

834
00:59:57,161 --> 00:59:58,421
Are we all supposed to die?

835
01:00:01,088 --> 01:00:03,308
Go. We'll talk at home.

836
01:00:04,794 --> 01:00:07,272
I can't study because of you.

837
01:00:07,275 --> 01:00:09,368
The kids are still bawling their eyes out.

838
01:00:09,454 --> 01:00:11,600
How are you going to fix this mess?

839
01:00:11,614 --> 01:00:13,834
It's a lie, right? Admit it.

840
01:00:14,782 --> 01:00:17,534
Fine. I lied.

841
01:00:18,507 --> 01:00:21,651
Like you said, 24 hours isn't enough
just to get by,

842
01:00:22,880 --> 01:00:24,793
so how would I ever date anyone?

843
01:00:24,818 --> 01:00:26,484
And even if I did,

844
01:00:27,662 --> 01:00:29,381
who would marry someone like me?

845
01:00:29,406 --> 01:00:31,028
Have you lost your mind?

846
01:00:31,188 --> 01:00:32,868
How could you lie about that?

847
01:00:33,722 --> 01:00:35,127
I was so worn down.

848
01:00:36,582 --> 01:00:38,338
So sick of all of it.

849
01:00:38,779 --> 01:00:40,881
I just wanted to run away. So what?

850
01:00:41,281 --> 01:00:44,724
You get to live just fine
in your 1,500-dollar blouse,

851
01:00:44,749 --> 01:00:47,512
so why am I the only one
stuck with all this misery,

852
01:00:47,644 --> 01:00:49,787
wondering how long this has to go on?

853
01:00:49,961 --> 01:00:51,932
It was suffocating. I was losing it.

854
01:00:51,935 --> 01:00:53,908
That's just your lot in life.

855
01:00:54,015 --> 01:00:55,741
You were born that way. What can you do?

856
01:00:58,108 --> 01:01:00,049
Is that how you talk to your sister?

857
01:01:01,164 --> 01:01:02,370
Have some manners.

858
01:01:03,955 --> 01:01:06,528
Was that directed at me? And so casually?

859
01:01:12,028 --> 01:01:13,349
The guy from the bus stop?

860
01:01:13,803 --> 01:01:15,954
- Gyu Yeong.
- Talk down to me too, if it bugs you.

861
01:01:16,768 --> 01:01:19,294
- And who are you?
- The man marrying your sister.

862
01:01:22,852 --> 01:01:25,496
You said it was all a lie.

863
01:01:25,521 --> 01:01:27,362
It may be a lie to your sister,

864
01:01:27,909 --> 01:01:29,052
but I mean it.

865
01:01:29,513 --> 01:01:30,548
What now?

866
01:01:34,515 --> 01:01:35,948
Please stop here. I mean it.

867
01:01:38,175 --> 01:01:39,839
My family is poor,

868
01:01:40,600 --> 01:01:42,236
I have no savings,

869
01:01:42,957 --> 01:01:44,831
four younger siblings to support,

870
01:01:45,619 --> 01:01:46,930
and I never went to college.

871
01:01:48,098 --> 01:01:49,241
I have no mother,

872
01:01:50,695 --> 01:01:53,025
and my father comes home
once every few months,

873
01:01:54,259 --> 01:01:56,535
so my siblings have only me.

874
01:01:58,908 --> 01:02:00,132
Choosing me,

875
01:02:01,200 --> 01:02:04,295
is the worst hand
you could possibly pick up.

876
01:02:05,275 --> 01:02:08,489
If I turn selfish,
I could cling to you and never let go.

877
01:02:10,062 --> 01:02:11,216
So,

878
01:02:11,450 --> 01:02:13,985
unless you want to sink
into the muck with me,

879
01:02:14,593 --> 01:02:16,808
count yourself lucky and run.

880
01:02:17,208 --> 01:02:18,216
No.

881
01:02:19,577 --> 01:02:20,688
I'm not running.

882
01:02:25,294 --> 01:02:26,689
Muck or anywhere else,

883
01:02:28,317 --> 01:02:30,533
I'll go wherever you are,

884
01:02:32,241 --> 01:02:33,728
so don't think about running.

885
01:02:37,581 --> 01:02:39,528
Quite the scene you two are making.

886
01:02:41,788 --> 01:02:43,828
If you've heard enough,
would you give us some space?

887
01:02:45,088 --> 01:02:46,096
And if I do?

888
01:02:46,184 --> 01:02:48,395
- What will you two do?
- What do you think?

889
01:02:48,397 --> 01:02:49,941
We're two people in love.

890
01:02:51,141 --> 01:02:54,534
If you're into watching,
feel free to stay.

891
01:03:08,401 --> 01:03:09,501
Gyu Rim,

892
01:03:13,575 --> 01:03:14,841
may I hold you?

893
01:03:17,895 --> 01:03:18,954
Say so if you'd rather not.

894
01:04:18,710 --> 01:04:21,923
(Love on the Menu)

895
01:04:22,168 --> 01:04:26,241
- He's Gyu Rim's boyfriend.
- Gyu Rim is dating someone?

896
01:04:26,348 --> 01:04:28,091
She landed a real catch.

897
01:04:28,093 --> 01:04:29,838
Did he lie about being broke?

898
01:04:29,869 --> 01:04:32,863
- It's a knockoff.
- A knockoff? Who's he conning?

899
01:04:32,888 --> 01:04:35,999
- He's me in my younger days.
- Mu Jin is different.

900
01:04:36,009 --> 01:04:37,694
He's not the type to lie.

901
01:04:37,695 --> 01:04:39,872
In case Gyu Rim panics and runs.

902
01:04:39,874 --> 01:04:42,046
- If I lose Gyu Rim like this,
- I'm sorry.

903
01:04:42,048 --> 01:04:43,115
I'll regret it my whole life.

904
01:04:43,117 --> 01:04:47,472
Give up everything you enjoy
because of me, or give up that girl.

905
01:04:47,475 --> 01:04:48,510
Han Gyu Rim.

906
01:04:49,017 --> 01:04:50,065
I love you.

907
01:04:50,727 --> 01:04:51,748
Mu Jin.

908
01:04:52,371 --> 01:04:54,071
Dramaday.me
